      "title": "Re-check: address vs. contents",
      "lede": "A cell's address and its contents are two different things — here is the contrast.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_spreadsheet_grid_references.r01.b1",
          "role": "misconception",
          "text": "The address B2 is the cell's location — column B, row 2. The contents of B2 is whatever you have typed or calculated there: a number, a city name, or a formula. Changing the contents does not change the address; B2 is always B2 regardless of what is inside it.",
          "lineage": {
