          "block_id": "tile_spreadsheet_grid_references.r03.b1",
          "role": "misconception",
          "text": "To reference all cells in row 5, write 5:5 — the row number on both sides of the colon. To reference all cells in column H, write H:H — the column letter on both sides. This is different from a rectangular range like A10:E20, which uses different start and end addresses. H:H always expands as new rows are added.",
